{"type":"assistant","uuid":"a17cc4fa-2fcb-40d4-a68b-e65a8d27c330","session_id":"fb96d7ea-0174-4ed7-95fe-bd8c14973064","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"a17cc4fa-2fcb-40d4-a68b-e65a8d27c330","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear understanding of the bug. Let me trace through the code:\n\n1. The `typeSpinner` uses `R.array.new_file_types` as its data source (4 items: Markdown, Plaintext, Todo.txt, None)\n2. The `new_file_types__file_extension` array maps to the same indices (`.md`, `.txt`, `.todo.txt`, empty)\n3. When the dialog opens:\n   - `fileExtEdit.setText(appSettings.getNewFileDialogLastUsedExtension())` - restores the last extension used\n   - But `typeSpinner` is never updated, so it stays at position 0 (Markdown)\n\nThe fix: After setting the extension in `fileExtEdit`, I need to look up the extension in `typeSpinnerToExtension` and call `typeSpinner.setSelection(index)` to sync the spinner with the restored extension. Now I'll implement this fix.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1ce47faa-6eef-4810-bf97-97722e5b1320","session_id":"fb96d7ea-0174-4ed7-95fe-bd8c14973064","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1ce47faa-6eef-4810-bf97-97722e5b1320","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI now fully understand the bug. Let me verify by checking the exploration agent and then implement the fix.\n\nThe bug is clear:\n\n1. When the dialog opens, `fileExtEdit.setText(appSettings.getNewFileDialogLastUsedExtension())` restores the last-used extension (e.g., `.todo.txt`)\n2. However, the `typeSpinner` is **never** updated to match the restored extension — it always starts at position 0 (Markdown)\n3. The spinner items (`R.array.new_file_types`) and the extension array (`R.array.new_file_types__file_extension`) are parallel arrays with the same indices\n\nThe fix is to look up the last-used extension in the `typeSpinnerToExtension` array and set the spinner position accordingly.\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
