{"type":"assistant","uuid":"7432aad5-e3d8-4e7f-b658-a06e7e05717f","session_id":"fb96d7ea-0174-4ed7-95fe-bd8c14973064","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"7432aad5-e3d8-4e7f-b658-a06e7e05717f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nHere's a summary of the bug and the fix:\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `NewFileDialog.java`, when the dialog opens:\n- `fileExtEdit` is correctly restored with the last-used extension (e.g., `.todo.txt`)\n- The `typeSpinner` is **never updated** — it stays at position 0 (Markdown)\n- The result: the extension field says `.todo.txt` but the type spinner says \"Markdown\"\n\n## The Fix\n\nAdded code to look up the last-used extension in the `typeSpinnerToExtension` array and set the spinner position to match:\n\n```java\nString lastExt = appSettings.getNewFileDialogLastUsedExtension();\nif (lastExt != null && !lastExt.isEmpty()) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < typeSpinnerToExtension.length; i++) {\n        if (lastExt.equals(typeSpinnerToExtension[i])) {\n            typeSpinner.setSelection(i);\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe spinner sync happens **after** the selection listener is attached, using the existing `typeSpinnerNoTriggerOnFirst` guard so the listener doesn't override `fileExtEdit` back when it fires.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The project's build environment lacks network access to download Gradle dependencies (`Connect to maven.google.com:443 failed`), so a full build cannot be run in this environment. However, the code is syntactically valid Java with no new imports or API changes.\n- The patch file has been saved to `new_file_dialog_type_spinner_fix.patch`."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45653,"output_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":44016,"total_tokens":46002}}}
